# ZvenFit — core rules

Static site built by Astro into `dist/`: pages in `src/pages`, shared markup in
`src/layouts` and `src/components`, data in `src/content` and `src/data`, classic
browser scripts in `src/scripts`. No client framework on pages (an island needs a
justification in the PR). Do not assume React or Next.

Release A is in progress on branch `feature/astro-release-a` (plan
`docs/astro-migration.md`, ADR `knowledge-base/decisions/002-astro-migration.md`):
after A1 only the legal pages are Astro pages; `public/**`, `scripts/snippets/**`,
`scripts/*.config.json` and `scripts/build-static.cjs` are frozen (hotfixes only).
Source: `src/`, `scripts/`, `functions/`. **Never edit `dist/` or `.astro/`.**

After changes: `npm run build` or `npm run dev:astro`; verify with `npm run check`,
`npm run lint`, `npm run test:build`. Parity with the legacy base: `npm run compare:dist`.

## APIs (endpoints built from env)

- Lead: `functions/lead-intake/` → `src/pages/js/lead-config.js.ts` → `window.ZVENFIT_LEAD_API`
- Schedule: `functions/fitbase-schedule/` → `src/pages/js/schedule-config.js.ts` → `window.ZVENFIT_SCHEDULE_API`
- Page views: `functions/site-traffic/` → `src/pages/js/traffic-config.js.ts` → `window.ZVENFIT_TRAFFIC_API`

## Shared markup

Menu, footer, analytics, Open Graph, JSON-LD and app badges are components in
`src/components/` rendered by `src/layouts/Base.astro`. Their whitespace is part of
the parity contract: Prettier is off for `src/layouts`, `src/components` and
`src/pages`. Comments inside component children are dropped by the compiler (use
`set:html`), raw non-breaking spaces become plain spaces (use `&nbsp;`).

## Brand

Keep green `#00d10e`, Roadrage + Roboto. See `TODO.md` "Out of scope".

## Secrets

No tokens in HTML/JS. Use env / GitHub Secrets only.

## Deploy

**Frontend (`zvenfit-frontend` bucket):** only via GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/main.yml`).
Do **not** manually upload to `zvenfit-frontend` (`yc storage s3api put-object`, `aws s3 cp/sync`, etc.) unless the user explicitly asks.

A push to `main` starts a release: staging deploy and E2E first, then production (`npm run build`, `s3 sync ./dist`). Work on a branch and open a pull request; during branch A stacked PRs target `feature/astro-release-a`.

**Assets bucket (`zvenfit`):** coach images and static CDN assets — not deployed by CI; manual ops only when the user requests or approves.
